  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "The paper introduces HeatCast, a Landsat-based benchmark dataset and evaluation harness for monthly Land Surface Temperature (LST) forecasting at 30 m resolution across 124 U.S. cities from 2013 to June 2025. It evaluates a CNN+LSTM model and Earthformer on next-month forecasting, finding that Earthformer achieves a 7.74 K RMSE, and that forecasting from eight non-LST channels alone (such as elevation and spectral indices) yields a 7.72 K RMSE.",
      "why": "It establishes the first shared, high-resolution benchmark for neighborhood-scale urban heat forecasting, replacing fragmented, single-city studies with a standardized dataset and evaluation framework across over a hundred cities."
    }
